WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
SpaceX reports starship pad construction at Kennedy Space Center nearly complete with acceptance testing now underway. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 124. Construction of structures and systems at KSC pad 39A is complete, and acceptance testing has begun. Director of NASA Science and Dragon Programs, Juliana Scheiman, said the team is moving from main construction into proofing and activation testing. Starship will fly from Texas at least

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.140
once more before attempting a Florida launch.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:39.600
Work is also advancing on towers at Cape Canaveral, SLC37A, and SLC37B.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:45.720
SpaceX is constructing three pads along Florida's coast, two at Cape Canaveral, and one

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.380
at NASA's Kennedy Space Center.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.020
The company holds a long-term lease with NASA to launch Falcon 9 and Falcon Heavy from

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:56.660
Pad 39A, now being expanded for Starship.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:02.700
As of today, Starship has launched on 14 integrated test missions from Starbase in Texas.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:08.640
According to StarLust, Musk posted that certain oligarchs are maintaining a monopolistic

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.640
chokehold and called the situation a crime against the Indian people.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:19.020
India's Ministry of Communications stated the regulatory framework is fair and non-discriminatory,

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.680
and that Starlink and two other licensed operators are at the same stage awaiting security assessments

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:30.680
before Spectrum assignment. Starlink has already installed more than 20 gateway sites and hundreds

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:36.640
of antennas in the country while meeting data sovereignty rules. Lauren Dreyer, Starlink's vice

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.900
president of business operations, said at the India Mobile Congress that the company stands ready

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:48.580
to serve India and wants to help achieve universal connectivity. Starlink has obtained GMPCS

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:54.020
authorization from the Department of Telecommunications but still needs final security clearances

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:59.820
and Spectrum. Reliance Geo and Barti Airtel have resisted administrative assignment of

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:05.440
satellite spectrum in favor of auctions. The Dragon spacecraft will lift off no earlier

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:11.800
than 6.33 a.m. Eastern daylight time on a Falcon 9 from Cape Canaveral with the final pair

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:18.880
of ISS rollout solar arrays. A backup window is available at 6.08 a.m. on October 14.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:24.160
The arrays will augment station power ahead of the plan 2030 de-orbit.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:30.380
Dragon will dock autonomously around 11 a.m. on October 15th and remain at the station

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.480
until mid-November.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:38.020
Live streaming of pre-launch activities begins at 6.15 a.m. eastern daylight time on the

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.240
NASA YouTube channel.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:45.700
The Expedition 75 crew will load the spacecraft with unneeded cargo and prime sensitive science

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.340
experiments before undocking.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:54.580
The system now uses multiple AI models, including competitors, when they deliver better answers for specific queries.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:03.080
SpaceX's GROC bot is shifting toward model routing that incorporates clawed and mid-journey outputs for improved results on certain tasks.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.660
The change reflects ongoing work to optimize inference across available frontier models.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:14.460
The financing would support one of the largest debt transactions tied to AI infrastructure growth.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.640
SpaceX is in talks with banks and investors to raise the funds specifically to purchase

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.380
and video chips for expanding compute capacity.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:28.020
The proposed deal underscores the capital demands of the current AI boom across technology

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:28.640
companies.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:34.460
The auction could benefit SpaceX along with Amazon and AST for satellite services.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:40.000
The Federal Communications Commission is set to vote on auctioning the band, which operators

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.080
view as valuable for next-generation satellite connectivity.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:50.280
Space X, Amazon, and AST have all expressed interest in the frequencies for their respective constellations.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.940
The vehicle completed a 2.5-month ocean voyage and is back at the Texas facility.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:03.140
Recovery teams brought the upper-stage home after it spent 75 days at sea following its most recent flight test.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:09.420
The return allows engineers to inspect hardware and continue iterative improvements on the Starship design.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:15.280
Dredges are operating at the freshwater inlet and SpaceX has begun permitting for an elevated

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.720
four-lane access road and bridge upgrades. The company announced plans for a new complex

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.580
in Vermilion Parish that could support high launch cadence. Early site work includes

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:32.400
road improvements on law 3147 and evaluation of nearby private landing strips for future support

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:38.720
operations. Observers note the third attempt at a Vandenberg Falcon 9 launch of reconnaissance satellites

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.360
is scheduled after two scrubs. The mission carries national security payloads and has already

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:50.620
faced two weather-related delays. Community members highlight Starship 40's return to Texas after

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:57.320
75 days at sea following its ocean recovery. The upper stage is now back at Starbase for post-flight

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:03.760
analysis and potential reuse in future tests. FCC approval of 15,000 next-generation

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.300
Starlink satellites for mobile service draws discussion on direct to cell competition.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.760
The satellites are designed to operate in the same spectrum bands used by terrestrial carriers.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:19.080
Reddit users track early permitting and road work at the planned Louisiana star-based site.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:24.400
Dredging at the freshwater inlet appears to be pre-scheduled activity that predates the formal

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.400
announcement. One thing worth watching is that India's three licensed satellite operators,

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:34.460
including Starlink, must still complete security assessments and obtain spectrum assignments

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:39.680
before any can begin commercial service. The Ministry of Communications emphasized that

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:45.120
all three licensees remain at broadly the same regulatory stage. On the AI front,

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:50.080
Grokbot now roots queries across multiple models, including Claude and mid-journey

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:55.240
when they provide stronger results for a given task. The routing approach allows the system

00:05:55.240 --> 00:06:00.220
to select the best performing model per query rather than relying on a single architecture.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:06.560
SpaceX continues to integrate these capabilities as part of its broader pivot toward AI infrastructure.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.300
The engineering angle on the final Irosa solar arrays centers on how roll out flexible

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:17.940
blankets solve mass and volume constraints that rigid panels cannot meet at the same power

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:18.280
level.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:24.360
Each array deploys from a compact canister using stored strain energy in the mass and blanket.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:29.200
it, avoiding the need for heavy motors or hinges that would add mass to every resupply

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:29.660
flight.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:35.460
The design trades initial complexity in the deployment mechanism for a power to mass ratio

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:40.280
that supports the station's growing experiment load and eventual controlled deorbit.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:46.520
At roughly 20 kilowatts per pair once installed, the arrays reduce reliance on the original

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:50.780
rigid arrays whose degradation has already limited available power margins.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:56.440
The choice also reflects a broader pattern in which SpaceX and NASA favor lightweight

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:01.940
deployables that fit inside Dragon's trunk volume rather than requiring dedicated heavy

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:04.220
lift flights solely for power hardware.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:09.680
This approach keeps the marginal cost of each additional kilowatt low enough that the

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:15.580
station can maintain operations through 2030 without a full redesign of the power architecture.

